V. 8, 9, 10 The Je••ſh Rabbis were alſo called Father and Maſter, by their ſeveral D•ſ•iples, whom they required,
1. To believe implicitly what they affirmed, without aſ••ing any farther Reaſon;
2. To obey implicitly what they enjoin••, without ſeeking farther Authority. Our U••d therefore by forbidding us either to give or receive the Title of Rabbi, Maſter, or F•th•, for••ds us either to receive any ſuch Reverence, or to pay any ſuch, to any but GOD.
